meta {
  name: Update Rules (admin, tenant-wide)
  type: http
  seq: 35
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hr/attendance/rules/admin
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "geofence_enabled": true,
    "geofence_radius_meters": 200,
    "require_photo": true,
    "require_geo": true,
    "allow_wfh_checkin": false,
    "regularization_max_backdate_days": 15,
    "regularization_approval_levels": 2,
    "scope": "tenant"
  }
}

docs {
  Writes the TENANT-WIDE default row (hr.attendance_rules with org_id NULL) that
  every org without its own override inherits. Orgs that already have their own
  row keep it — precedence is whole-row, org over tenant.

  EXPECT 403 unless the caller's platform_role is tenant_admin or super_admin:
    "Only tenant admins can set attendance rules for every organization"
  The hr.attendance.admin capability alone is NOT enough. It says "may configure
  attendance"; writing the row other orgs inherit is a tenancy question, so an
  org's own hr_admin cannot reconfigure its siblings.

  Omit "scope" (or send "org") to write only the calling org's override — that is
  what Update-Rules-Admin.bru does and what the default is.
}
